+# CONTRACT — Beam Splitter
+
+Implementation in `src/index.ts`, exporting `countBeamCells(grid: string[][]): number`
+and `countBeamPaths(grid: string[][]): bigint`.
+
+## Beam model
+
+A beam state is `(row, col, dir)` where `dir ∈ {D, DL, DR}` with column deltas
+`D=0, DL=-1, DR=+1`. Rows always increase by 1 per step (DAG, no cycles).
+A beam *entering* cell `(r,c)` with direction `dir`:
+- out of bounds → the beam has exited (one complete path).
+- `grid[r][c] === '^'` → splits into `(r+1, c-1, DL)` and `(r+1, c+1, DR)`.
+- otherwise → continues to `(r+1, c+Δdir, dir)`.
+Source `'S'` emits a downward beam (`D`) entering its own cell.
+
+## countBeamCells
+
+- [ ] Returns count of distinct in-bounds cells visited by any beam -> test: example 1 → 5
+- [ ] Two-splitter example: overlapping landing cell counted once -> test: example 2 → 6
+- [ ] Source cell counts as visited -> test: grid with S, no splitter → equals rows traversed
+- [ ] Splitter cell hit by beam counts as visited -> test: example 1 includes (2,1)
+- [ ] Beam straight down with no splitter visits one cell per row in that column -> test: 5x3 single column → 5
+- [ ] Beam exiting sides/bottom does not count out-of-bounds cells -> test: splitter at edge, no negative cols counted
+- [ ] No source → 0 -> test: grid of all '.' → 0
+- [ ] Cell visited by multiple beams via different directions counted once -> test: convergent beams → unique count
+- [ ] Multiple 'S' sources all emit -> test: two sources → union of their cells
+- [ ] Empty grid / empty rows → 0 -> test: [] and [[]] → 0
+
+## countBeamPaths
+
+- [ ] Counts distinct source-to-exit beam paths as bigint -> test: example 1 → 2n
+- [ ] Each splitter doubles branch count -> test: example 2 → 4n
+- [ ] Absorbed (out-of-bounds) beams still count as exited paths -> test: example 2 includes (3,-1) path → 4n
+- [ ] No splitter → 1 path -> test: single column grid → 1n
+- [ ] No source → 0n -> test: all '.' grid → 0n
+- [ ] Distinct paths landing on same cell counted separately -> test: example 2 (two paths to (3,1)) → 4n
+- [ ] Multiple sources sum their paths -> test: two sources → sum
+- [ ] Large result fits bigint (K splitters → up to 2^K) -> test: diagonal cascade of splitters → 2^K
+
+## Performance
+
+- [ ] 200x200 grid, 50 splitters resolves < 5s for both functions -> test: timed validation
+
+## Quality gates
+
+- [ ] `npm test` passes
+- [ ] `npm run build` clean
+- [ ] `npm run lint` clean
